3. Coupled Dynamics and Reduced Model

The full state vector evolves according to a controlled stochastic differential equation with jumps:

dX(t)=F\bigl(X(t),u(t),d(t)\bigr)\,dt
+\sigma\bigl(X(t)\bigr)\,dW(t)
+\int_{\mathbb R^q} J\bigl(X(t),z\bigr)\,\tilde N(dt,dz),

where:

· F is the deterministic drift,
· u(t)\in U is the control vector,
· d(t)\in D is the external disturbance vector,
· \sigma(X)\,dW represents continuous stochastic fluctuations,
· \tilde N(dt,dz) is a compensated Poisson random measure with intensity \lambda(X)\nu(dz),
· J(X,z) is the jump amplitude.

The control vector is

u(t)=
\begin{bmatrix}
u_E\\ u_T\\ u_C\\ u_I\\ u_S
\end{bmatrix},

representing interventions in energy, technology, knowledge, institutions, and safety.

3.1 Reduced model

The full seven-dimensional state is not yet numerically tractable. For illustration and future computation, we define a reduced state

z(t)=
\begin{bmatrix}
g(t)\\
c(t)\\
e(t)
\end{bmatrix},

where:

· g(t) is a scalar genetic adaptive load or selection-pressure index,
· c(t) is the effective cultural-technological knowledge stock,
· e(t) is environmental stress.

The variables I, R, and A enter as control and coupling parameters rather than as independent states.

A minimal coupled system is

\begin{aligned}
\frac{dg}{dt}
&=
\alpha_g(c,e)-\mu_g g+\sigma_g \xi_g(t),\\
\frac{dc}{dt}
&=
\alpha_c(c,I,R,A)-\mu_c c+\sigma_c \xi_c(t),\\
\frac{de}{dt}
&=
\alpha_e(c,T,A)-\mu_e e+\sigma_e \xi_e(t)+j_e\,dN_e(t).
\end{aligned}

A concrete linear-quadratic instantiation is

\begin{aligned}
\frac{dg}{dt}
&=
a_{g0} - \beta_g g + \gamma_g e + \sigma_g \xi_g,\\
\frac{dc}{dt}
&=
a_{c0} + \beta_c c\left(1-\frac{c}{K_c}\right) + \eta_c I + \theta_c A - \mu_c c + \sigma_c \xi_c,\\
\frac{de}{dt}
&=
a_{e0} - \gamma_e c + \delta_e e - \zeta_e T + \sigma_e \xi_e + j_e\,dN_e.
\end{aligned}

Here:

· \beta_c is the logistic growth rate of the knowledge stock,
· K_c is the carrying capacity of the knowledge stock,
· \eta_c is the institutional transmission coefficient,
· \theta_c is the AI augmentation coefficient,
· \gamma_e is the environmental benefit of knowledge,
· \zeta_e is the environmental benefit of technology,
· j_e\,dN_e is an environmental shock term.

No viability kernel is computed in this manuscript. The computational plan is specified in Section 9.

