4. Timescale Separation and Domain-Specific Adaptive Acceleration

Biological evolution, cultural evolution, and technological evolution operate on different characteristic timescales.

Let:

· \tau_G be the characteristic time for substantial biological evolutionary change,
· \tau_C be the characteristic time for significant cultural change,
· \tau_T be the characteristic time for significant technological change.

We hypothesize that modern technological civilization is characterized by

\tau_T \ll \tau_C \ll \tau_G

for many adaptive domains. This is an empirical hypothesis, not a universal law.

4.1 Operational definition of \tau_G

For a biallelic locus under selection coefficient s and generation time g_T, the deterministic time for an allele to rise from frequency 0.1 to 0.9 is

\tau_G = \frac{\ln 81}{s}\, g_T.

If multiple loci are involved, an effective selection coefficient s_{\mathrm{eff}} is used.

4.2 Operational definition of \tau_C and \tau_T

For a cultural trait or technology, \tau_C or \tau_T is defined as the time from 10\% to 90\% adoption in a specified population, estimated from logistic diffusion curves.

For logistic diffusion with rate r,

\tau_C
=
\frac{\ln 81}{r_C},
\qquad
\tau_T
=
\frac{\ln 81}{r_T}.

4.3 Effective cultural-technological timescale

The effective cultural-technological adaptation timescale is provisionally defined by the parallel combination

\tau_{C+T}^{-1}
=
\tau_C^{-1}
+
\tau_T^{-1},

so that

\tau_{C+T}
=
\frac{\tau_C \tau_T}{\tau_C+\tau_T}
\le
\min(\tau_C,\tau_T).

This formula is justified if cultural and technological adaptation act as independent parallel channels with additive rates. It is not justified if the channels are sequential or strongly coupled. In sequential cases, \tau_{C+T}\approx \max(\tau_C,\tau_T). In redundant cases, \tau_{C+T}\approx \min(\tau_C,\tau_T). Because the parallel formula is the most optimistic of these three, it should be treated as a lower bound on the effective timescale, not as a universal fact.

The proposed empirical program should therefore report:

· \tau_{C+T}^{\mathrm{parallel}} using the formula above,
· \tau_{C+T}^{\mathrm{max}}=\max(\tau_C,\tau_T) as a conservative alternative,
· \tau_{C+T}^{\mathrm{min}}=\min(\tau_C,\tau_T) as a redundant-channel lower bound.

The domain-specific ratio should be computed under all three alternatives.

4.4 Domain-specific adaptive timescale separation ratio

Because culture and technology do not have a single speed, we define a family of domain-specific ratios. For each adaptive domain k,

\Lambda^{(k)}(t)
=
\frac{\tau_G^{(k)}(t)}{\tau_{C+T}^{(k)}(t)}.

When \Lambda^{(k)}\gg 1, adaptive change in domain k occurs predominantly through cultural and technological mechanisms rather than through genetic change.

The central falsifiable hypothesis is that

\Lambda^{(k)}(t)\text{ has increased from }<1\text{ in the Pleistocene to }\gg 1

for selected adaptive domains in the Anthropocene. This is not claimed to hold uniformly across all traits, populations, or environments.

4.5 Illustrative cross-domain comparison

This calculation is illustrative only. It is not an empirical estimate of a universal \Lambda.

For lactase persistence, selection coefficients estimated from ancient DNA are roughly s\sim 0.02–0.06 per generation. With a generation time of g_T\approx 25 years, the characteristic genetic timescale is

\tau_G = \frac{\ln 81}{s}g_T
\approx \frac{4.394}{0.02\text{--}0.06}\times 25
\approx 1{,}800\text{--}5{,}500\text{ years}.

For modern communication technology, global mobile cellular subscriptions rose from roughly 10\% to 90\% penetration in about 15 years. Taking \tau_T\approx 15 years and \tau_{C+T}\approx \tau_T, the contrast is

\Lambda \approx \frac{1{,}800\text{--}5{,}500}{15}
\approx 120\text{--}370.

Thus, for this specific cross-domain comparison, \Lambda\sim 10^2. This supports the hypothesis that selected domains of modern technological civilization operate in a regime where cultural-technological adaptation dominates genetic adaptation. It does not imply that all genetic adaptation has stopped, nor that all cultural traits diffuse at this speed.

