Appendix E. Reduced Toy Model and Viability Constraints

The full seven-dimensional state

X=(G,C,T,E,I,R,A)

is not yet numerically tractable for viability-kernel computation. We therefore define a reduced three-dimensional state

z(t)=
\begin{bmatrix}
g(t)\\
c(t)\\
e(t)
\end{bmatrix},

where:

· g(t) is a scalar genetic adaptive load or selection-pressure index,
· c(t) is the effective cultural-technological knowledge stock,
· e(t) is environmental stress.

The variables I, R, and A enter as coupling parameters and controls rather than as independent states.

A minimal coupled system is

\begin{aligned}
\frac{dg}{dt}
&=
\alpha_g(c,e)-\mu_g g+\sigma_g \xi_g(t),\\
\frac{dc}{dt}
&=
\alpha_c(c,I,R,A)-\mu_c c+\sigma_c \xi_c(t),\\
\frac{de}{dt}
&=
\alpha_e(c,T,A)-\mu_e e+\sigma_e \xi_e(t)+j_e\,dN_e(t).
\end{aligned}

A concrete linear-quadratic instantiation is

\begin{aligned}
\frac{dg}{dt}
&=
a_{g0} - \beta_g g + \gamma_g e + \sigma_g \xi_g,\\
\frac{dc}{dt}
&=
a_{c0} + \beta_c c\left(1-\frac{c}{K_c}\right) + \eta_c I + \theta_c A - \mu_c c + \sigma_c \xi_c,\\
\frac{de}{dt}
&=
a_{e0} - \gamma_e c + \delta_e e - \zeta_e T + \sigma_e \xi_e + j_e\,dN_e.
\end{aligned}

Here:

· \beta_c is the logistic growth rate of the knowledge stock,
· K_c is the carrying capacity of the knowledge stock,
· \eta_c is the institutional transmission coefficient,
· \theta_c is the AI augmentation coefficient,
· \gamma_e is the environmental benefit of knowledge,
· \zeta_e is the environmental benefit of technology,
· j_e\,dN_e is an environmental shock term.

The viability region for the reduced model is provisionally defined as

\mathcal V_{\mathrm{red}}
=
\left\{
(g,c,e)\in\mathbb R^3:
g\le g_{\max},\quad
e\le e_{\max},\quad
c\ge c_{\min}
\right\}.

The parameters g_{\max}, e_{\max}, and c_{\min} are provisional and must be estimated independently. They are not to be fitted to collapse events.

